## Node 1 is the only node that runs.  Nodes 2 and 3 are fictitious:
## node 2 is the neighbor named by the egress plan, node 3 is the
## destination.  Because node 3 is not a neighbor, ipnfw must consult
## the contact plan to reach it -- a static plan to the destination
## would bypass CGR, and with it the copy counter, entirely.
1 1 config.ionconfig
s
m horizon +0
m clockerr 0

a range +0 +3600 1 2 1
a range +0 +3600 2 3 1

## The second hop is always available, so a route to node 3 exists for
## as long as some 1->2 contact does.
a contact +0 +3600 2 3 100000

## A run of brief 1->2 contacts, each separated from the next by a gap.
## Nothing can be transmitted (the plan has no outduct), so every one of
## these closes on the bundles still queued and re-forwards them onto the
## next contact.  There are more contacts here than MAX_XMIT_COPIES.
a contact +12 +14 1 2 100000
a contact +15 +17 1 2 100000
a contact +18 +20 1 2 100000
a contact +21 +23 1 2 100000
a contact +24 +26 1 2 100000
a contact +27 +29 1 2 100000
a contact +30 +32 1 2 100000
a contact +33 +35 1 2 100000
a contact +36 +38 1 2 100000
a contact +39 +41 1 2 100000
a contact +42 +44 1 2 100000
a contact +45 +47 1 2 100000
a contact +48 +50 1 2 100000
a contact +51 +53 1 2 100000
a contact +54 +56 1 2 100000
a contact +57 +59 1 2 100000
a contact +60 +62 1 2 100000
a contact +63 +65 1 2 100000
a contact +66 +68 1 2 100000
a contact +69 +71 1 2 100000
a contact +72 +74 1 2 100000
a contact +75 +77 1 2 100000
a contact +78 +80 1 2 100000
a contact +81 +83 1 2 100000
